title text_grid -- the terminal grid meets the pixel family, GREEN
prompt Autonomous loop: read the road-ahead docs, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first optimizing for the balance compass, deep-read one council-rota doc, send often, stop at custody gates.
think Read the three road docs (1024-round itinerary, eight-season double-seat, rye-first crypto wave) and the REMEMBER INNER LOOP live edge. The open-media font family is very deep (~20 font laps); the prior lap closed the Scooter write loop as a balance pivot. Crypto stands WHOLE (do not reopen without a named gap). Balance compass wants a rung that unites families rather than one more leaf.
think Surveyed both families: the terminal grid (scooter_view.Frame is 24x80 bytes; dexter_line; scooter_compose) and the open-media paint family (font5x7_ascii, text_paint, qoi). Grepped image/ and pond/apps/ -- no module paints a terminal frame into an image. The two families were built side by side and had never met on metal. That gap is the highest-Lindy crux: the bridge every future glass surface (Grainphone, Realidream, Skate) stands on to render a terminal to pixels.
think Layering care: the Frame type lives in pond/apps (pond composes image, never the reverse). So the painter must NOT import scooter -- it paints ANY monospace byte grid. Built image/text_grid.rye: a generic grid->image painter, pure composition over glyph/color/qoi/text_layout/text_paint/font5x7_ascii. The pond glue (feed a live Frame's cells, already []u8 of the same shape) is a later one-line rung.
think Design: col_pitch = font_ascii.glyph_advance (every ASCII glyph shares the advance, so a laid row is naturally monospace, column c at c*pitch). paint_grid checks the whole grid's box against the target ONCE up front (all-or-nothing, GridOutOfBounds by name), then paints each row via text_layout.layout_line + text_paint.paint_placed stepping down by one cell height. render_grid is the verb a surface reaches for: allocate a bg-filled canvas sized exactly to the grid (bounded by qoi_max_pixels, GridTooLarge by name), paint fg, return the Pixmap.
think Witness crux -- faithful BY MEASURE not claim: built a real terminal-shaped grid (the exact bytes scooter_view.Frame.cells carries -- a header row, a post row, a blank row) as plain bytes; proved the painted ink equals the summed glyph coverage of every non-space cell exactly, the blank row is ground byte-for-byte, a chosen cell's pixel block equals a standalone glyph paint at its grid origin, the render is deterministic, and the image round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte. Mis-shapes (GridCellsMismatch, BadGridDims, GridOutOfBounds) each refuse by name leaving the buffer untouched.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red: a 16x3 grid painted into a 96x21 image, ink 291 px equal to the summed cell coverage. First hitch was the TAME compound-assert ban (assert(a and b)); split into single asserts, each with its own positive invariant. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, both new files plain 7-bit ASCII.
obs Balance lap held: a bridge that JOINS the terminal family and the open-media paint family, rather than a twenty-first leaf font -- the harmony compass over raw font throughput. Correctly layered so image/ stays self-contained; the pond bridge is trivial and deferred.
obs Rota this lap (d27) deep-read item 18, context/TWO_ROOMS.md -- the checkable and the visionary. This rung is pure checkable room: every claim (ink count, byte-for-byte round-trip, cell-block parity, named refusals) is bound by the witness on metal, none borrowed from narrative. The bridge crossed from vision to checkable by exactly one door -- a green witness.
loom witness=text_grid_witness grid=16x3 image_px=96x21 ink_px=291 wall_ms=NA
file image/text_grid.rye the monospace grid->image painter: paint_grid (all-or-nothing) and render_grid (the surface verb), pure image-family composition
file tools/text_grid_witness.rish proves the bridge faithful by measure, deterministic, QOI-round-tripping, and refusing every mis-shape by name
file image/README.md accreted the text_grid entry naming the terminal-meets-pixels bridge role and the faithful-by-measure crux (docs-sync)
file crux/REMEMBER.md INNER LOOP live edge + Git nib refreshed to name the text_grid bridge rung
recommend keep-going the pond bridge rung (scooter_paint: feed a live scooter_view.Frame's cells to render_grid, showing a real conversation as an image) is the natural next mechanical lap; still no seam, no gate.
